---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="About" description={SITE.description} quiet>
  <div class="wrap about">
    <header class="page-head rise">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Kerem Altaylar</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede">
          Kerem Altaylar is a sound artist, researcher and performer based in
          Istanbul. He composes for multichannel and immersive systems, builds the
          software instruments his work depends on, and studies the sonic ecologies
          that connect the two.
        </p>

        <p>
          His compositional work is concerned with listening at the threshold —
          with <strong>microsoundscapes</strong>, environments whose events are too
          quiet, too small or too slow to register under ordinary conditions.
          Amplified, time-scaled and diffused across a multichannel array, these
          materials shift from background to architecture, and the listener's
          relationship to them inverts.
        </p>

        <p>
          That practice is inseparable from the tools it requires. He works as an
          audio programmer across Web Audio, SuperCollider, Max and JUCE, designing
          digital instruments, generative engines and real-time systems — including
          a series of browser-based instruments and machine-listening tools. The
          instrument and the composition tend to develop together: each piece
          establishes what the system needs to do, and the system in turn determines
          what the piece can become.
        </p>

        <p>
          As a performer he works with live electronics, live coding and drumming,
          at the intersection of generative systems and rule-based improvisation. He
          has performed at Sonified, Sonar Istanbul, Arter and Algorave Istanbul, and
          at Hochschule für Musik, Hannover.
        </p>

        <p>
          He is a PhD candidate in Sonic Arts at Istanbul Technical University's MIAM
          (Center for Advanced Studies in Music), where his research addresses
          biomultisensography and transductional sonic ecologies: how signals move
          between organic and technical systems, and what is gained and lost in each
          translation.
        </p>

        <h2>Areas of work</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Multichannel and spatial composition</li>
          <li>Sonic ecologies, bioacoustics and microsoundscapes</li>
          <li>Digital instrument design and audio programming</li>
          <li>Generative systems, artificial life and live coding</li>
          <li>Live electronics and improvisation</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <aside class="contact">
        <h3>Contact</h3>
        <p><a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></p>

        <h3>Follow</h3>
        <ul class="links">
          {SITE.follow.map((l) => (
            <li><a href={l.href} rel="me noopener">{l.label} →</a></li>
          ))}
        </ul>

        <h3>Also</h3>
        <ul class="links">
          <li><a href="https://www.fxhash.xyz/u/Kerem%20Altaylar" rel="noopener">fxhash →</a></li>
        </ul>

        <p class="cv-link"><a href="/cv/">Full CV →</a></p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 6rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
  }
  .page-head h1 {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 16rem;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    opacity: 0.9;
  }
  .contact {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--bdr);
    padding-top: 1.2rem;
    position: sticky;
    top: 6rem;
  }
  .contact h3 {
    margin-block: 1.8rem 0.7rem;
  }
  .contact h3:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .contact p,
  .links a {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }
  .links {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }
  .links a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
  }
  .cv-link {
    margin-top: 2.2rem;
    padding-top: 1.2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--bdr);
  }
  .cv-link a {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .contact {
      position: static;
    }
  }
</style>
